            <trans-unit id="VNxe2Mo">
                <source>description.guided_project_social_google_reviews</source>
                <target>Connect the listing's Google profile, then display its reviews on the site.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="FrDtWdT">
                <source>description.guided_project_social_links</source>
                <target>One single list for the whole site, rendered wherever the social links block is put</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="GjyFwm5">
                <source>description.guided_project_social_share_buttons</source>
                <target>Pick the networks offered to your visitors, their order and their look</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="Q2.88W1">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_google_connect</source>
                <target>In the sidebar's "Advanced" submenu, click "Connect Google", then grant access with the Google account owning the listing. The site stores the token, the account and the listing by itself.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="XzEU5fT">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_google_credentials</source>
                <target>Search for "social-google-oauth-client-id" and "social-google-oauth-client-secret" in the list, and paste the two values taken from the Google Cloud console. The three other Google keys fill themselves in at the next step.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="RJQ_vuA">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_google_display</source>
                <target>On the page you want, add a "Collection" block and pick the "Customer reviews" source. Reviews are shown with their rating, their date and the link to the original review.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="6xgYazB">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_google_prerequisites</source>
                <target>This first part happens at Google and takes 7 to 10 business days: access to the Business Profile API, then publishing the OAuth app. The help procedure "Display your listing's Google reviews" gives the links and the exact order. Come back here once access is granted.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="cFM7OuY">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_google_reply</source>
                <target>Only the public reply is written here, and it goes to Google as soon as it is saved. The review's text and rating belong to its author: they can be neither edited nor deleted. An abusive review is reported to Google.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="pu1hp1o">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_google_reviews</source>
                <target>Reviews come in with the "c975l:social:reviews:sync" command, to be scheduled once a day. The list stays empty until it has run.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="vgXH0gX">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_links_display_label</source>
                <target>Unchecked, the name is still read by screen readers: it leaves the screen, never the accessibility.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="TOBz.H3">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_links_edit</source>
                <target>Create it if it does not exist yet, open it otherwise: there is only one for the whole site.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="ajiJRR8">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_links_entries</source>
                <target>One row per network: its icon, the address of your page over there, and a label if you want to replace the network's own.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="CbQbxws">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_links_icon_style</source>
                <target>Plain icon, badge in the network's own colors, a ring filling in on hover, or text only with no icon. The preview right below shows the result.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="XKnrijD">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_links_intro</source>
                <target>Optional: a line above the icons, inviting visitors to follow you. Left empty, nothing at all is rendered.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="IiZiN6F">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_links_open</source>
                <target>Your networks are not page content: they are entered once here, and the site picks them up everywhere.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="qTr5m1O">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_links_place</source>
                <target>Add the social links block to a page or to the footer: it renders this list, wherever it sits.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="i3T88kV">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_share_buttons_anchor</source>
                <target>Optional: a short id ("share") so a menu entry can point straight at the band. Without an anchor, it is still reached by scrolling the page.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="qRGp6fm">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_share_buttons_check</source>
                <target>Open any published page: the buttons are there, with the look you have just given them. Hovering the band raises a button bringing you straight back here.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="XoOi0Jd">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_share_buttons_display_intro</source>
                <target>The "share this page" line above the buttons: its wording is the site's own, only its display is set here.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="dcxhtln">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_share_buttons_edit</source>
                <target>Create them if they do not exist yet, open them otherwise: there is only one set for the whole site.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="k0_UuQi">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_share_buttons_fill</source>
                <target>The preview right below updates on every change, before anything is even saved.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="XwJ3XNI">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_share_buttons_networks</source>
                <target>Tick the ones you want, and drag them: the order of the list is the order shown.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="LxtX23p">
                <source>description.guided_step_social_share_buttons_open</source>
